1. What is TCP/IP Model?
Definition

The TCP/IP Model is a 4-layer networking model that explains how data travels from one device to another over the Internet.

Simple Definition

TCP/IP is the set of rules that allows computers to communicate over the Internet.

Why do we need TCP/IP?

Without TCP/IP:

❌ No Google
❌ No WhatsApp
❌ No YouTube
❌ No Online Banking

It is the foundation of the Internet.

Real-Life Example

Suppose you search "www.google.com".

Your request goes through the TCP/IP layers:

You
↓

Application Layer

↓

Transport Layer

↓

Internet Layer

↓

Network Access Layer

↓

Internet

↓

Google Server

Google sends the response back using the same layers in reverse order.
