7. Data Flow in TCP/IP

Suppose you open www.youtube.com

Step 1: Application Layer

You type the website address.

↓

Step 2: Transport Layer

TCP divides the data and ensures reliable delivery.

↓

Step 3: Internet Layer

IP finds the best route to YouTube's server.

↓

Step 4: Network Access Layer

Data travels through Wi-Fi or Ethernet.

↓

Internet

↓

YouTube Server

The response comes back using the same layers in reverse.

