1. What is an IP Address?
Definition

IP (Internet Protocol) Address is a unique number given to every device connected to a network.

Simple Definition
An IP Address is the address of a device on a network.

Just like your house has an address,

Every computer/mobile also has an address.

That address is called an IP Address.

Real-Life Example

Suppose you order food from Zomato.

The delivery boy needs your home address.

Without your address,
he cannot deliver the food.

Similarly,

When Google sends data,
it needs your device's address.
That address is called the IP Address.

Example
Laptop
IP = 192.168.1.5

Mobile
IP = 192.168.1.6

Printer
IP = 192.168.1.10

Every device has a different IP.

Why do we need an IP Address?

Without an IP Address,

Google won't know where to send data.
WhatsApp messages won't reach you.
YouTube videos won't load.
⭐ Interview Answer
An IP Address is a unique logical address assigned to every device on a network. It helps identify devices and enables communication over a network.

2. Types of IP Address

There are 2 versions.

IPv4
IPv6

3. IPv4
Definition
IPv4 is the older and most commonly used version of IP.

Structure

IPv4 contains 32 bits.
It is divided into 4 parts (octets).

Example

192.168.10.5

Each part ranges from:

0 – 255
Example
192

168

1

10

These are called Octets.

Why only 0–255?

Each octet contains 8 bits.

Maximum value of 8 bits

11111111

↓

255
Interview Question

How many bits are there in IPv4?

Answer
32 bits

4. IPv6
Definition

IPv6 is the new version of IP.

Why was IPv6 introduced?

Because IPv4 addresses were running out.

The number of Internet users became very large.

So a bigger address space was needed.

Structure

IPv6 contains

128 bits

Example

2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7334

Don't memorize the format.

Just remember

128 bits

