Before TCP sends data,

both computers first say

"I'm ready."

Step 1

Client

↓

SYN

"I want to connect."

Step 2

Server

↓

SYN + ACK

"Okay, I'm ready."

Step 3

Client

↓

ACK

"I'm also ready."

Connection starts.

