1. HTTP (HyperText Transfer Protocol)
Simple Definition

HTTP is a protocol used to open websites and transfer web pages between your browser and a web server.

Real-Life Example

You open:

www.google.com

Your browser sends an HTTP request, and Google sends back the webpage.

Port Number

80

Interview Definition

HTTP is an application layer protocol used to transfer web pages and data between a client (browser) and a web server.

2. HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure)
Simple Definition

HTTPS is the secure version of HTTP. It encrypts data so that hackers cannot easily read it.

Real-Life Example

When you log in to:

Gmail
Amazon
Online Banking

HTTPS keeps your password and personal information secure.

Port Number

443

Interview Definition

HTTPS is a secure version of HTTP that uses encryption (TLS/SSL) to protect data exchanged between the client and the server.

3. FTP (File Transfer Protocol)
Simple Definition

FTP is used to upload and download files between a computer and a server.

Real-Life Example

A web developer uploads website files from their computer to a hosting server.

Port Number

21

Interview Definition

FTP is an application layer protocol used to transfer files between a client and a server.

4. TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)
Simple Definition

TCP makes sure that all data reaches the destination correctly and in the right order.

Real-Life Example

When you transfer money using online banking, you cannot lose any data. TCP ensures reliable delivery.

Used For
Banking
Email
File Downloads
Online Shopping
Interview Definition

TCP is a reliable, connection-oriented transport layer protocol that ensures data is delivered correctly and in the correct order.

5. UDP (User Datagram Protocol)
Simple Definition

UDP sends data quickly without checking whether every packet reaches the destination.

Real-Life Example

During a video call, if one video frame is lost, the call continues instead of waiting for that frame.

Used For
Video Calls
Online Games
Live Streaming
DNS
Interview Definition

UDP is a fast, connectionless transport layer protocol that sends data without guaranteeing delivery.

6. IP (Internet Protocol)
Simple Definition

IP helps data travel from one network to another using IP addresses.

Real-Life Example

Google Maps finds the best route to a destination.

Similarly, IP helps data find the route to another device.

Interview Definition

IP is a network layer protocol responsible for addressing and routing packets between networks.

